<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Treasury Hldgs buys Gen Accident portfolio.</title>
<headline>Irish Treasury Hldgs buys Gen Accident portfolio.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish-based property investment firm Treasury Holdings Ltd on Tuesday said it had entered into a joint venture to buy a UK-based property portfolio from General Accident for 62.465 million sterling.</p>
<p>Treasury Holdings said in a statement that its joint venture partner was EX Lands Properties Plc.</p>
<p>The GA portfolio consists of a diversified portfolio of 41 properties with long unexpired lease terms.</p>
<p>The current net income from the portfolio, which includes tenants such as the UK government, Bank of Ireland, Burtons, Signet Group OLC, British Heart Foundation, is in excess of six million sterling per annum.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
</text>
